# Build-time config for the deployed app.
#
# Committed deliberately. Both values are PUBLIC BY DESIGN: Vite inlines them
# into the JavaScript bundle, so anyone who opens devtools on the deployed site
# can read them whether or not this file is in the repo. Hiding them in a CI
# secret would be theatre.
#
# They are safe because of RLS (supabase/schema.sql): `anon` has no read and no
# write. Verified against a live row — an anonymous SELECT returns [] with data
# present, and an anonymous INSERT returns 401.
#
# The sb_secret_... key is the opposite and must never appear here.
# To rotate: change the value below, or set SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_ANON_KEY as
# GitHub repository variables, which the deploy workflow prefers when present.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://dzkqzrmnnucpqfeydghl.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_1A_-GLNXsGYMLAIOnfk4Hw_RotDg5xv
